From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaid <283011337+nottzaid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Water: transmission and flowing foam

PBRAppearance.transmission: a thin clear surface with water's Fresnel
(IOR 1.333), blended premultiplied so the bed shows through, no
refraction offset. PBRAppearance.flowFoam: the source river's foam
recipe (4D and 3D fractal noise, its scales, distortion, ramps and
24 fps drivers) along the UVs, animated by simulation time. The foam is
white and opaque, and its bump blends with the flat normal by the Bump
node's strength, as in the source.

Replaces these patches of the numbered series, with what each measured
as it landed (tools/profile_forest.py, GTX 1060 3 GB, i5-4670):
- 0010-transmission-and-flow-foam: the river's pixels only
- 0019-white-foam
